        "id": 212177,
        "name": "WalkingTarget",
        "username": "WalkingTarget",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/walkingtarget/{size}/4833_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-01-02T15:57:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Phantom5613\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/48/1906_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Phantom5613:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I must admit, I don't really know what a 'midwestern' accent sounds like…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Honestly, while there are regional variations within the large area known as the \"Midwest\", it's essentially what you'd hear on American TV all the time. The \"General Midwestern American\" accent is most notable for it's <em>lack</em> of major regional markers which makes it a good one to emulate for TV or movies.</p>\n<p>Edit for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ntLTSIjFgrw\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">example</a>!</p>",
